formal land tenure:It's a Partially,Data exists mainly on state property that contains specific maps. The National Institute of Statistics (INE) lists Neighborhood Units grouped by sectors. In these sectors, you can see the number of private and collective dwellings, but there is no lotification of the properties. This data was extracted from the 2017 Population and Housing Census. No specific map of land tenure types was found. Some data are divided by gender, but not necessarily those referring to land property. There are maps of the country's indigenous territories, but no maps of Afro-Chilean territories could be found.;
communal land tenure:It's a Partially,https://www.arcgis.com/apps/dashboards/83f2649bd32a44f8b75da18542dac0a8;
land tenure on indigenous people or ethnic minorities:It's a Partially,The Neighborhood Units, present in the National Institute of Statistics portal, offer information on the number of traditional Indigenous dwellings in a neighbourhood unit. The Ministry of Public Works provides seven maps of indigenous territories in the country. No map of the Afro-Chilean territories was observed.;
informal land parcels:It's a Yes,The Open Geodata, a section of the website of the National Institute of Statistics (INE) offers a study of the 2020-2021 Campamentos. In Chile, the term “campamentos” refers to areas of poverty formed by informal settlements. This study shows a graph of informal settlements between 1930-2020. Documents on this study, divided into case studies in the national territory, are available. Documents can be downloaded in pdf, excel, and a zip file with documents gdb table, spx, freelist. There is a lot of metadata.;
leasehold/concession rights:It's a Yes,There is a map of Fiscal Properties of the Department of Spatial Data Infrastructure of Chile. The following map contains information on fiscal properties subject to and having some administrative act, such as leases, concessions, destinations, easements, occupancy permits, and affectations.

