formal land tenure:There is a Cadastre searchable map to find information about urban and rural parcels, and statistical data on urban and rural plots including the names of the owners, the area and the value of the plots.;
communal land tenure:The National Colonisation Institute, which manages public land for its collective use through two forms of production units (Family Production Units - UPF and Associative Production Units - UPA), provides data on land access, the beneficiaries of its policies, number of units, area and location.;
land tenure on indigenous people or ethnic minorities:Uruguay does not have native indigenous peoples.;
informal land parcels:There is information on informal settlements.;
leasehold/concession rights:The National Colonisation Institute provides data on the beneficiaries of its policies, their ages and distribution in the national territory and data on land allotments by type of production unit.

